# HurufPad — project rules

Source of truth for product: `docs/PRODUCT_BRIEF.md`. Follow that brief; do not add out-of-v1 features unless asked.
Visual / UI source of truth: `docs/DESIGN.md`. Use tokens in `src/index.css` and `src/theme/tokens.ts`; do not invent one-off colors or control styles.

## Stack

- React + TypeScript + Vite. No backend in v1; static host only.
- Canvas of **letter and scribble sticker objects** (e.g. Konva), not a single text field.
- PWA: cache the app so the board works offline after first load.
- Persistence: last board only, in `localStorage` / IndexedDB. No login, no cloud sync.

## Scribbles and speech

- Never send strokes or images to a cloud OCR API.
- Convert raw ink to a scribble sticker after a short pause, with an optional “Make sticker.” Do not infer a letter from handwriting.
- Keyboard insert places a letter sticker on the board.
- TTS: Web Speech API (`speechSynthesis`). Language from the English / Indonesian toggle. Do not assume Indonesian voices exist on every device.

## Functional style

- Avoid classes and OOP (`class`, `extends`, `this` for domain logic). Prefer functions, plain data, and React function components + hooks.
- Model the board as data (arrays/records of board items) and pure functions that return new state. No mutable class stores.
- Side effects (canvas, IndexedDB, speech) live in small functions or hooks, not in class methods.
